            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a watchman, then the Telugu for a milkman."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఆలోచన",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆలోచన — ālōcana — \"an idea; a thought\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నాకు ఒక మంచి ఆలోచన వచ్చింది. nāku oka mañci ālōcana vaccindi. I had a good idea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ఆలోచనలు, ālōcanalu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An idea comes to you: నాకు ఆలోచన (ālōcana) వచ్చింది, literally an idea came to me."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆలోచన (ālōcana) is borrowed from Sanskrit ālocana, \"seeing\", and also \"considering, reflection\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
