          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దృక్పథం — dṛkpathaṁ — \"an outlook; a perspective\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ప్రతి మనిషికి ఒక దృక్పథం ఉంటుంది. prati maniṣiki oka dṛkpathaṁ uṇṭundi. Every person has an outlook."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A formal word for the way someone looks at life or at a question."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దృక్పథం (dṛkpathaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit dṛkpatha, \"the range of sight\" (Monier-Williams), a compound of dṛk-, from dṛś \"to see\", and patha, \"a path\" (CDIAL 7743)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
