          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కోణం — kōṇaṁ — \"an angle; a point of view\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మనం ఆ సమస్యను వేరే కోణం నుంచి చూడాలి. manaṁ ā samasyanu vērē kōṇaṁ nuñci cūḍāli. We should view that problem from a different angle."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: కోణాలు, kōṇālu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In geometry a corner or an angle; in talk, the side from which you see a question."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కోణం (kōṇaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit koṇa, \"a corner, an angle\" (Monier-Williams). Like many Sanskrit nouns in -a, it ends in -ం in Telugu."
            }
          ]
        },
